{
  "_comment": "Onboarding's feed picker (docs/milestones/cold-start-onboarding.md, decided 2026-10-18). Collected by the project, not a reader: only a publisher's own feed (a self-chosen host such as CNA's feedburner counts), never an RSS hub or a machine aggregator (Google News, Yahoo). A human-curated front page is collectable (owner, 2026-10-25): Hacker News through hnrss.org, a third-party feed of HN's front page kept on 2026-10-20 because HN has no feed of its own, and Techmeme, whose items link to its own page for each story and are kept as sent: its excerpt lets a reader decide, and that page links the cited article (owner, 2026-10-26). Every entry here passed both parsers (workers/rss/src/parse.js and feedparser, scripts/validate_feed_catalog.py) with at least one article inside 8 days when the validator last ran over it (2026-10-20; Techmeme, added after that run, on 2026-10-25 with `--only`). A wire service or breaking-news outlet carries the `news` tag (it keeps the article from the scorer, so the filter alone judges it, src/cyris/domain/tags.py); an analysis or tech-trade outlet does not. `topics` is the list's own grouping, not a `SourceConfig` field: the ordered table at the top names each subject (what a feed is about, never its form, so news, columns and blogs mix within one), and each feed names one or two of its ids. The wizard shows the topics first and only the chosen topics' feeds, and strips `topics` from an entry before posting it; `tags` still go into the pipeline and are never a topic. On 2026-10-20 the owner widened the list toward blogs and columns, keeping every earlier entry: the science topic and 35 feeds came from a research pass that validated them, and their tags were cut back to the pipeline's existing words (news, tech, startup, opinion, analysis, investigative), since a topic, not a tag, says what a feed is about. Read once at onboarding by the wizard's sources step, through GET /api/onboarding/feeds; after that a deployment's feeds live in its own `sources` (D1) or `sources.yaml`, and adding one is the existing single-source form, not this file.",
